      <memberdef kind="define" id="group__safe__data__container__apis_1ga44ad4716f7743e811a5547a1e8009a4f" prot="public" static="no">
        <name>SAFE_SECTION</name>
        <param><defname>_c</defname></param>
        <param><defname>_pvar</defname></param>
        <initializer>for (int _sd_st = ((z_safe_lock(_SAFE_LOCK(_c)) == 0)                  \
           ? <ref refid="group__safe__data__core__apis_1ga08da109c60349a5bd8f6fbe8af830704" kindref="member">safe_data_verify_repair</ref>(&amp;(_c)-&gt;<ref refid="structpayload" kindref="compound" external="/wrk/z/ws-safety/bdoc-toolbox-r3a/deploy/html/dox-safe-data-testspec/doxygen.tag">payload</ref>,           \
                    sizeof((_c)-&gt;<ref refid="structpayload" kindref="compound" external="/wrk/z/ws-safety/bdoc-toolbox-r3a/deploy/html/dox-safe-data-testspec/doxygen.tag">payload</ref>), (_c)-&gt;_crc, \
                    _SAFE_SHADOW(_c))                  \
           : (z_safe_data_lock_failed(), -ETIMEDOUT));         \
     /* enter on valid (0) or recovered (-EAGAIN) */                   \
     ({ bool _ok = (_sd_st == 0 || _sd_st == <ref refid="group__safe__data__core__apis_1ga2e449be977ff002accc60ffdacd439d6" kindref="member">SAFE_DATA_RECOVERED</ref>);     \
    if (!_ok &amp;&amp; _sd_st != -ETIMEDOUT) {                            \
        z_safe_unlock(_SAFE_LOCK(_c));                         \
    }                                                              \
    _ok; });                                                       \
     z_safe_data_seal(&amp;(_c)-&gt;<ref refid="structpayload" kindref="compound" external="/wrk/z/ws-safety/bdoc-toolbox-r3a/deploy/html/dox-safe-data-testspec/doxygen.tag">payload</ref>, sizeof((_c)-&gt;<ref refid="structpayload" kindref="compound" external="/wrk/z/ws-safety/bdoc-toolbox-r3a/deploy/html/dox-safe-data-testspec/doxygen.tag">payload</ref>),           \
              &amp;(_c)-&gt;_crc, _SAFE_SHADOW(_c)),                  \
     z_safe_unlock(_SAFE_LOCK(_c)), _sd_st = 1)                        \
    for (__typeof__((_c)-&gt;<ref refid="structpayload" kindref="compound" external="/wrk/z/ws-safety/bdoc-toolbox-r3a/deploy/html/dox-safe-data-testspec/doxygen.tag">payload</ref>) *_pvar = &amp;(_c)-&gt;<ref refid="structpayload" kindref="compound" external="/wrk/z/ws-safety/bdoc-toolbox-r3a/deploy/html/dox-safe-data-testspec/doxygen.tag">payload</ref>;        \
         _pvar != NULL; _pvar = NULL)</initializer>
        <satisfies>
          <requirement refid="requirement_SD-REQ-021"></requirement>
        </satisfies>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Scoped lock + verify ... reseal + unlock around a block. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Inside the block, <computeroutput>_pvar</computeroutput> is a typed pointer to the (verified) payload and may be used with plain C syntax. On normal exit the integrity tag is resealed and the lock released. This is the ergonomic, leak-free replacement for the original &quot;checkout pointer / remember to update&quot; pattern.</para>
<para>The block is entered only if the pre-check passes (or the data was recovered from the shadow copy). On an unrecoverable fault the block is skipped and the lock is released; the configured fault action has already run inside <ref refid="group__safe__data__core__apis_1ga5a7ff94945a049416e8edc6f0d3f019a" kindref="member">safe_data_verify()</ref>.</para>
<para><programlisting><codeline><highlight class="normal">SAFE_SECTION(&amp;cfg,<sp/>p)<sp/>{</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>p-&gt;temperature<sp/>=<sp/>90;</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>p-&gt;fan_enabled<sp/>=<sp/>(p-&gt;temperature<sp/>&gt;<sp/>85);</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">}</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting></para>
<para><simplesect kind="note"><para>Do not <computeroutput>return</computeroutput>/<computeroutput>break</computeroutput>/<computeroutput>goto</computeroutput> out of the block: that would skip the reseal+unlock. <computeroutput>continue</computeroutput> is fine (it exits the block normally).</para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="note"><para>Uses GNU C extensions (statement expressions, <bold>typeof</bold>) and hides control flow in a macro - only available with CONFIG_SAFE_DATA_GNU_EXTENSIONS (off at the Strict level). SAFE_UPDATE gives the same atomicity guarantee in standard C.</para>
</simplesect>
The block is also skipped (and the lock-timeout event reported) when the container lock cannot be acquired within CONFIG_SAFE_DATA_LOCK_TIMEOUT_MS.</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>_c</parametername>
